==========================================================================
THE POINT (Vitali): measure cannot distinguish these three at the core
==========================================================================
  At the regular polygon the OPEN lonely set is EMPTY (measure 0) and the CLOSED
  lonely set is exactly the n-gon vertices {k/n} (n points, measure 0, NONEMPTY).
  Measure assigns 0 to: the empty set, the n points, and the boundary of any
  positive set -- it CANNOT see nonemptiness here. The Vitali set is the extreme:
  a nonempty/full transversal with NO well-defined measure. So a measure tool
  (S550's resonance energy E) is intrinsically blind to the measure-zero core.

  RESOLUTION: LRC's core is NOT Vitali-pathological -- it is measure-zero but
  EXPLICITLY CONSTRUCTIBLE. The SIEVE (THM-369) exhibits the rational witness
  t = a/q (no axiom of choice): a constructive choice of the relevant Q-coset
  representatives. Measure (S550) handles the decorrelated bulk; the sieve handles
  the measure-zero core. The Vitali set marks exactly the handoff: where measure
  ends, explicit (arithmetic) construction must begin.

  ADELIC echo (S547): the Vitali quotient R/Q lives at the ARCHIMEDEAN circle;
  LRC's tight witnesses are the RATIONAL points (the line<->tree diagonal). Measure
  is an archimedean (line) tool; the core's witnesses are rational (diagonal) -- the
  sieve is the p-adic/tree-side construction. Vitali = the measure-blindness of the
  line at its own rational points = where the tree (sieve) must take over.
